<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10395" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conquīsītĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		conquiro, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a seeking</i> or <i>search for, a
				bringing together, procuring, collecting</i> (rare, but in good
			prose). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pecuniarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. H.
					2, 84</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(sacrorum),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Agr. 6
						<i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">difficillimum est in omni conquisitione
					rationis exordium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Univ. 2 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">piaculorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					7, 3, 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Milit. t. t.</b>, <i>a levying,
			levy</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Prov. Cons. 2, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 23,
				32, 19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">25, 5,
				9</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">intentissima,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 29, 35, 10 al.</span></i>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
